# DNA-AND content · the grand tour: one flight from the whole visible universe down to the quarks, for watching
# Run it: Universe.exe --tour grand-tour (or DNA-AND.exe --tour grand-tour). Any key or click takes the controls back.
# Edit the stops to make your own. Each @stop home
do: pick
target: home-galaxy
caption: Home

@stop open
do: arc
rate: -0.06
until-km: 2e18
turn: 2.5
seconds: 6
caption: We begin at home: our galaxy, a hundred billion stars turning in the dark

@stop leave
do: zoom
rate: -0.3
until-km: 5e21
caption: Every point of light out here is a whole galaxy

@stop web
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 7
caption: The cosmic web: galaxies along filaments, round vast empty voids

@stop choose-galaxy
do: pick
target: galaxy
caption: A galaxy

@stop to-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 1.5e18
caption: We fall toward one galaxy among a hundred billion

@stop round-galaxy
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 8e17
turn: 3
seconds: 5
caption: A hundred billion stars round a giant black hole

@stop into-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 1e16
caption: Into it: the glow breaks into stars, each with worlds of its own

@stop bh
do: pick
target: black-hole
caption: A black hole

@stop to-bh
do: zoom
rate: 1.0
until-km: 3e4
caption: A star crushed to nothing: a black hole

@stop round-bh
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 3
seconds: 6
caption: Its pull bends the light of the stars behind it; from inside its horizon nothing escapes

@stop choose-star
do: pick
target: star
caption: A star

@stop into-system
do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 3e11
caption: One star among them

@stop arrive-system
do: arc
rate: 0.3
until-km: 3e9
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Circling in: the star, and the worlds born round it

@stop round-system
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 5
caption: Each world on its own tilted orbit

@stop asteroid
do: pick
target: asteroid
caption: An asteroid

@stop to-asteroid
do: zoom
rate: 0.6
until-km: 300
caption: Out to its belt of rubble

@stop round-asteroid
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 4
seconds: 4
caption: An asteroid: rock left over from when the worlds were made

@stop comet
do: pick
target: comet
caption: A comet

@stop to-comet
do: zoom
rate: 0.9
until-km: 1e4
caption: Out to the Oort cloud, a light-year from the star

@stop round-comet
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 4
seconds: 4
caption: A comet: ice and dust that has waited out here since the worlds were made

@stop star-2
do: pick
target: star
caption: Another star

@stop to-star-2
do: zoom
rate: 0.55
until-km: 3e11
caption: Across light-years to another star

@stop arrive-star-2
do: arc
rate: 0.3
until-km: 3e9
turn: 3
seconds: 7
caption: Circling in on its worlds

@stop round-star-2
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 4
caption: Another system, its worlds on their own orbits

@stop choose-planet
do: pick
target: planet
caption: A world

@stop to-planet
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 2e4
caption: Down to one of its worlds

@stop round-planet
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 1.5e4
turn: 3
seconds: 6
caption: Seas, land, clouds and a thin shell of air

@stop to-land
do: zoom
rate: 0.55
until-km: 1.5
caption: Down through the air to the land

@stop over-hills
do: glide
rate: 0.5
turn: 1.5
seconds: 8
caption: Hills raised by moving plates, valleys worn by water

@stop to-head-height
do: zoom
rate: 0.3
until-km: 0.002
caption: Down to where a person stands

@stop stand
do: pick
target: none
caption: Standing

@stop look-up
do: look
tilt: 55
turn: 1.5
seconds: 5
caption: Look up

@stop sky
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 5
caption: Our star, the other worlds, the galaxy's stars beyond

@stop look-down
do: look
tilt: -85
turn: 1
seconds: 5
caption: And down: there is as much below us as above

@stop to-grains
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 2e-6
caption: The ground breaks into stones, then grains of sand

@stop to-face
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 2e-9
caption: Onto one grain, a crystal of one mineral

@stop round-face
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 4
caption: Its face: steps, cracks, clay plates, a film of water

@stop to-crystal
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 6e-12
caption: Down to its atoms

@stop round-crystal
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 3
caption: Atoms in a pattern repeated billions of times

@stop choose-atom
do: pick
target: atom
caption: One atom

@stop to-atom
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-13
caption: An atom is not a ball

@stop round-atom
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 2.5e-13
turn: 4
seconds: 6
caption: A tiny nucleus, its electrons round it on tilted paths

@stop to-neighbour
do: pick
target: bonded-atom
caption: Its neighbour

@stop across-bond
do: arc
rate: 0.0
until-km: 0
turn: 4
seconds: 5
caption: Across the bond to its neighbour: atoms share their outer electrons

@stop to-next-atom
do: pick
target: bonded-atom
caption: The next atom

@stop round-next-atom
do: arc
rate: 0.0
until-km: 0
turn: 4
seconds: 5
caption: Atom to atom through the crystal, each its own little system

@stop choose-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: One electron

@stop follow-electron
do: orbit
turn: 2
seconds: 4
caption: An electron: a point, and a wave spread through its cloud

@stop choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Inward: an atom is almost all empty space

@stop round-nucleus
do: arc
rate: 0.03
until-km: 1.2e-17
turn: 2.5
seconds: 5
caption: Protons and neutrons, bound by the strong force

@stop choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: A proton

@stop to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a single proton

@stop round-proton
do: orbit
turn: 2.5
seconds: 5
caption: Three quarks in a storm of gluons

@stop choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: A quark

@stop to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.25
until-km: 6e-19
caption: One quark

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 1.5
seconds: 4
caption: The smallest thing we know. The same universe at every scale
